---
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout title="Documentation" description="Learn how Super ii accounts, organizations, public repositories, reviews, plans, and future publishing workflows work.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Documentation"
    title="Build in public with a clear path to release."
    description="The launch documentation covers what works today and labels the publishing capabilities that open after the first creator cohort."
    compact
  />

  <div class="shell content-shell">
    <article class="prose">
      <h2 id="start">Start here</h2>
      <p>Super ii is in public beta. You can create an account with email, Google, or GitHub, explore public repositories, search their metadata, join discussions, react, follow, watch, and curate collections.</p>
      <blockquote><p>Model, dataset, and app uploads stay closed until the separate Super ii Runtime reports local storage and both required scanners ready. Every revision also needs human approval before Postgres permits publication.</p></blockquote>

      <h2 id="account">Create an account</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Select <strong>Join free</strong> anywhere on the site.</li>
        <li>Continue with email, Google, or GitHub.</li>
        <li>Verify the address when prompted and complete your public profile.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The free plan requires no payment card. Authentication is provided through a dedicated Super ii application; account credentials are not stored in the website source.</p>

      <h2 id="catalog">Explore the hub</h2>
      <p>The three public catalogs are separated by the kind of work they contain:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/models">Models</a> hold immutable revisions, weights, configuration, cards, local analysis, licenses, lineage, and responsible-use notes.</li>
        <li><a href="/datasets">Datasets</a> hold schemas, bounded previews, licenses, provenance, data cards, and immutable files.</li>
        <li><a href="/spaces">Apps</a> hold reviewed Gradio projects and their project information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="architecture">Architecture</h2>
      <p>The Astro website on Cloudflare is the public control plane. Postgres stores version history, review evidence, full-text and trigram search, community state, collections, and lineage. A separately operated Linux runtime is the data plane for quarantine, content-addressed files, ClamAV, Gitleaks, offline format inspection, and optional local inference.</p>
      <p>No commercial inference API sits behind the tools. Browser inference uses local repository files and local Transformers.js WASM. Server inference is designed for operator-owned llama.cpp and optional Diffusers hardware. vLLM and semantic-search TEI remain explicitly deferred until dedicated capacity and measured search demand justify them.</p>

      <h2 id="capability-status">Capability status</h2>
      <p><strong>Implemented</strong> means the code, database contract, fail-closed controls, UI, and local-runtime path exist and pass the launch checks. It does not mean Super ii is pretending to operate hardware that is not connected: uploads and server inference stay closed until an always-on operator-owned Linux runtime independently reports its database, storage, ClamAV, and Gitleaks gates ready.</p>
      <div class="comparison-scroll">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Requested capability</th><th>Code status</th><th>Activation</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1 · Files, revisions, releases, tags, downloads, reviews, SHA-256 object storage; no Xet</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Runtime host required for uploads</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 · Safetensors validation and tensor metadata</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Automatic during model inspection</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3 · Datasets splits, schema, first 100 rows, and media previews rendered in Astro</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Automatic after approved upload</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4 · Offline Transformers model understanding</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Local files only; remote code disabled</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5 · Local tokenizer inspection and interactive token tool</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Shown on compatible public models</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6a · Browser Transformers.js, local WASM, WebGPU/WASM</td><td>Implemented</td><td>User device pays the compute cost</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6b · llama.cpp GGUF run, chat, settings, and token statistics</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Operator runtime hardware required</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7 · vLLM high-throughput serving</td><td>Deferred as requested</td><td>Only after dedicated GPU capacity</td></tr>
            <tr><td>8 · Offline Diffusers generation</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Optional runtime GPU/CPU dependencies required</td></tr>
            <tr><td>9 · Gradio repository, isolated container, app iframe</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Rootless Docker runtime required</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10 · Postgres full-text/trigram search and filters</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Active control-plane search</td></tr>
            <tr><td>11 · Text Embeddings Inference semantic search</td><td>Deferred as requested</td><td>Only after measured Postgres search limits</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12 · ClamAV quarantine gate</td><td>Implemented, fail closed</td><td>Fresh scanner service required</td></tr>
            <tr><td>13 · Gitleaks publication gate</td><td>Implemented, fail closed</td><td>Pinned local CLI required</td></tr>
            <tr><td>14 · Discussions, comments, reactions, events</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Active for public repositories</td></tr>
            <tr><td>15 · Likes, follows, watchers, activity</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Active for signed-in users</td></tr>
            <tr><td>16 · Mixed repository collections</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Active for signed-in users</td></tr>
            <tr><td>17 · Typed lineage and provenance graph</td><td>Implemented</td><td>Shown when verified relationships exist</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="publish">Publishing roadmap</h2>
      <p>An upload enters quarantine, receives path/MIME/hash validation, then must pass ClamAV, Gitleaks, format policy, and its applicable offline inspector. Clean bytes move into an immutable SHA-256 object store. A finalized manifest and human approval are required before the PL/pgSQL publication gate can make the revision public.</p>
      <p>An empty result means exactly what it says: no public item has been approved. There are no generated demo entries or simulated download counts.</p>

      <h2 id="organizations">Organizations</h2>
      <p>Organizations are shared identities for teams. Free accounts can participate in public community work. Paid team capabilities will add private repositories, richer roles, audit history, and shared billing when those features leave beta.</p>

      <h2 id="plans">Plans and usage</h2>
      <p><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> distinguishes the open Free plan from beta-waitlist and proposal plans. Storage, inference, endpoints, and accelerated app runtime will be usage-priced separately, with limits and spend controls shown before activation.</p>

      <h2 id="api">API status</h2>
      <p>The health endpoint is at <a href="/api/health"><code>/api/health</code></a>. Public search is available by repository kind, for example at <a href="/api/search?kind=model"><code>/api/search?kind=model</code></a>. Published file downloads and safe media previews, tokenizer requests, local browser-model files, llama.cpp, Diffusers, isolated Gradio app control/proxying, discussions, comments, reactions, likes, watches, follows, and collections use scoped server routes. State-changing and server-compute routes require a same-origin authenticated session, and resource-heavy work is rate limited.</p>

      <h2 id="support">Get help</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> for access, plan, enterprise, security, privacy, or launch questions. Please do not include secrets, credentials, private model files, or sensitive personal data.</p>
    </article>

    <aside class="prose-aside">
      <h2>On this page</h2>
